---
title: "Connect SillyTavern and other apps"
description: KoboldAI Lite is built in. To use KoboldCpp from SillyTavern or other apps, pick the right address - KoboldAI API, OpenAI-compatible /v1 or Ollama.
sidebar:
  label: "Connect other apps"
  order: 1
---

KoboldCpp has its own chat interface, KoboldAI Lite, at `http://localhost:5001`. You do not need another app. Connect one only if you prefer its interface or features.

## Which address to use

Start KoboldCpp with a model first. Then enter the address that matches the connection type you pick in the app:

| Connection type in the app | Address |
|---|---|
| KoboldAI or KoboldCpp | `http://localhost:5001` |
| OpenAI-compatible | `http://localhost:5001/v1` |
| Ollama | `http://localhost:11434` (start KoboldCpp on port 11434, [see below](#ollama-apps)) |

- If an app asks for the full KoboldAI API address, use `http://localhost:5001/api`.
- `localhost` only works on the PC that runs KoboldCpp. For a phone or another PC, see [Remote access](/docs/api/remote-access/).
- If you changed **Port:** on the **Network** tab (`--port`), use your port in place of `5001`.

When KoboldCpp is ready, the console shows the addresses:

```text {% title="Console" frame="terminal" %}
Starting Kobold API on port 5001 at http://localhost:5001/api/
Starting OpenAI Compatible API on port 5001 at http://localhost:5001/v1/
Starting llama.cpp secondary WebUI at http://localhost:5001/lcpp/
```

## API key

- **No password set:** if the app requires an API key, enter any text.
- **Password set:** enter your password as the API key. See [Passwords and security](/docs/api/passwords-and-security/).

## Model name

OpenAI-style apps often ask for a model name. KoboldCpp ignores it and always uses the model it has loaded, so any name works. `http://localhost:5001/v1/models` lists the loaded model.

The exception is router mode, where the model name selects which model to load. See [Admin mode](/docs/settings/admin-mode/).

## Reply length

Set the response length (max tokens) in the app. If the app does not send one, KoboldCpp uses **Default Gen Amt:** on the **Context** tab (`--defaultgenamt`, default 2048).

## SillyTavern

SillyTavern has its own connection type for KoboldCpp:

{% steps %}

1. In SillyTavern, click **API Connections** (the plug icon in the top bar).
2. Set **API** to **Text Completion** and **API Type** to **KoboldCpp**.
3. Enter `http://localhost:5001` in **API URL**.
4. If you set a password, enter it in **koboldcpp API key (optional)**.
5. Click **Connect**.

{% /steps %}

KoboldCpp understands the SillyTavern-specific sampler fields, such as banned strings.

SillyTavern can also use KoboldCpp for images when an image model is loaded, through the A1111/Forge or ComfyUI APIs. Use the same `http://localhost:5001` address. See [Image generation](/docs/features/image-generation/).

## Ollama apps

Apps that only speak the Ollama API look for it on port 11434.

{% steps %}

1. On the **Network** tab, set **Port:** to `11434`. On the command line, add `--port 11434`.
2. Launch. The console prints `Ollama Emulation is now available at port 11434.`
3. In the app, use `http://localhost:11434`.

{% /steps %}

If Ollama itself is running, it already uses port 11434 and KoboldCpp cannot start on it. Close Ollama first.

## Anthropic-API apps

KoboldCpp serves the Anthropic Messages API at `/v1/messages`. With a password, the app must send it as `Authorization: Bearer <password>`. KoboldCpp does not accept the `x-api-key` header that Anthropic clients normally use. Configure such apps to send a Bearer token. If an app can't, run KoboldCpp without a password only where no one else can reach it, for example with **Host:** set to `127.0.0.1`.

## Other apps and tools

- **KoboldAI Lite online:** the hosted copy at [lite.koboldai.net](https://lite.koboldai.net) can connect to your local KoboldCpp.
- **KoboldAI United and KoboldAI Client:** enter the KoboldAI API address.
- **Bundled interfaces:** besides KoboldAI Lite, KoboldCpp serves the llama.cpp WebUI at `/lcpp/`, the image interface at `/sdui` and the music and speech interface at `/musicui`. The last two only generate when the matching model is loaded. See [KoboldAI Lite](/docs/features/lite/).
- **KoboldCpp Agent:** the bundled coding agent connects to `http://127.0.0.1:5001/v1` by default. See [Agent](/docs/features/agent/).
- **GPTLocalhost:** a Microsoft Word add-in that uses KoboldCpp.
- **Speech-to-text clients:** KoboldCpp accepts WAV, MP3 and FLAC audio. WebM recordings are not supported. See [Speech-to-text](/docs/features/speech-to-text/).

